{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547902-is-vitel-the-antediluvian-lasombra","id":1547902,"title":"Is Vitel the Antediluvian Lasombra?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-22T17:24:38-08:00","id":1547902,"title":"Is Vitel the Antediluvian Lasombra?","content":"Here I am. So let's talk some lore, I was discussing with a friend of mine who proposed that instead of making Vitel a kind of &quot;Sybil's (perhaps unknowingly) pawn&quot; it's more interesting having him being the Antediluvian himself in a way. Then we were talking about the possibilities, we all know that, if we go into system-like things, Lasombra wouldn't need to really &quot;be Vitel&quot;, but possibly having Vitel so completelly under his control (and here we have the system-thing like Dominat 10 enabling you to basically &quot;turn someone in another copy of you&quot;, that is, &quot;another character for you to play with&quot;) that in the end it's the same idea. The fact that Vitel control one of the world's most important cities would put him into a very useful spot.<br /> <br /> As to me, as I told him, I don't see a problem with that per se, I just think that Sybil herself would be enough a scary thing, but if one wants to take it into yet another level, it can be interesting for some kind of stories. There are few things in the WoD that could work as a better example of Cosmic Horror&quot; than the Antediluvian of the Clan of shadows, that's for sure.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think about it? One interesting thing that this possibility does is work towards &quot;character's economy&quot;, in a way that Sybil would be yet another character to add to an already convoluted story. Anyway, I'm here to hear your thoughts on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T11:14:22-08:00","id":1547912,"title":"","content":"My ears are burning. Someone must be talking about me!<br /> <br /> Seriously tho, Its no secret MV is one of my favorite characters (peep the handle if you missed it) and frankly I'm ashamed I missed this possible angle on him for 3 decades. So, now that you've added some new fuel lets see what kind of plot hooks this arrangement (or even rumors of this arrangement) could kick up.<br /> <br /> 1) Vitel/Sybil's plan to use the United State nuclear arsenal to 'first strike' the Antediluvians. What if even THAT mad plan is only a cover or a first order result of (Lasombra)'s true plan. Not only would such a conflict destroy his competitors it could also lead to nuclear winter. And what is nuclear winter other than a great shadow encompassing the earth.<br /> <br /> I can't find the reference at the moment but, during the Dark Ages, didnt some Lasombra work with Malkavians in a plan to blot out the sun. This accomplishes the same goal without the (a) unreliable Malks or (b) unreliable mysticism.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;<i>You will rule again, as you were always meant to do. Destroy the lords who sought to combat you. You have the potential to become greater than your master. Use it wisely.&quot;</i> -- Sybil to Sejanus<br /> <br /> Lets look at this quote through the topsy-turvey set up you propose. We have a woman with the same name as a group of prophetesses speaking on the future of her childe (who may also be her sire via dominate shenanigans).<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You, (Lasombra), will rule again as you were almost meant to do. Destroy the (Ventrue) who sought to combat you. You have the potential to become greater than your (sire, Sybil). Use it wisely&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Kinda works perfectly with what you are proposing here especially with the V20 update of MV setting himself up as the independent &quot;Emperor&quot; of mid-atlantic Kindred.<br /> <br /> I'll probably have more later but I'm at work now and have to at least attempt to look busy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T11:28:10-08:00","id":1547913,"title":"","content":"It could work as the Lasombra wouldn't just rely on Grantino as one his proxies or puppets to accomplish his goals. I wouldn't be shocked if Sybil and Montono were primed for something similar. To be fair it wouldn't be shocking if the eldest direct childer or grandchilder would act as proxies for the antideuilvans various goals of trying to survive the war of ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-23-2025, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 