quote through the topsy-turvey set up you propose. We have a woman with the same name as a group of prophetesses speaking on the future of her childe (who may also be her sire via dominate shenanigans).<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You, (Lasombra), will rule again as you were almost meant to do. Destroy the (Ventrue) who sought to combat you. You have the potential to become greater than your (sire, Sybil). Use it wisely&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Kinda works perfectly with what you are proposing here especially with the V20 update of MV setting himself up as the independent &quot;Emperor&quot; of mid-atlantic Kindred.<br /> <br /> I'll probably have more later but I'm at work now and have to at least attempt to look busy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's indeed a very interesting idea to toy with Mr. Vitel. I'm now thinking about it, it gives a total new dimeension to the character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It could work as the Lasombra wouldn't just rely on Grantino as one his proxies or puppets to accomplish his goals. I wouldn't be shocked if Sybil and Montono were primed for something similar. To be fair it wouldn't be shocking if the eldest direct childer or grandchilder would act as proxies for the antideuilvans various goals of trying to survive the war of ages. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's for sure. Also plaing with this idea, makes the whole Jyhad a lot more scary. Since I was a kid I've always liked the idea that &quot;you're not sure who you're dealing with&quot;, as for instance a simple monk or even a beggar could be someone very important and powerful in desguise. <i>Lair of the Hidden</i> kind of plays with this idea with the &quot;Ghoul Stephen&quot; being in reality someone much scarier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T15:16:51-08:00","id":1547941,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, ther's another character who plays this very well and it's the &quot;Ghoul Izaha&quot;,a.k.a Elimelech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T11:43:25-08:00","id":1548063,"title":"","content":"I doubt it. There's a lot of Gratiano's arrogance and ambition within Vitel. The ol' Ante I believe already used that one, plus why be Vitel when he already is a pawn of his childe?<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T14:55:35-08:00","id":1548067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a hr